From 054a5c5f73848eb880f480925944f473efe837d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clifford Swartz <cliffordswartz1@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:25:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/57] hw/arm: add PIC32CM JH SoC and the pic32cm-jh01-cpro
 board

Peripheral Pretender v0, part A:
- mchp_regfile: byte-lane register-file dispatcher over the generated
  MchpRegInfo tables (mixed 8/16/32-bit registers, aliases, W1C,
  enable protection, debug-safe read side effects).
- mchp-regblock: generic peripheral built from one generated instance;
  every ATDF instance without a dedicated model uses it.
- Clock system (OSCCTRL, OSC32KCTRL, GCLK, MCLK) with ready bits and a
  Clock tree driving armv7m cpuclk (4 MHz at reset, 48 MHz after the
  Harmony init sequence).
- NVMCTRL, SUPC, RSTC (reset cause across resets), WDT (user-row reset
  values, CLEAR key), PM, PAC, DSU (DID, DSU_EXT mirror), DIVAS.
- SoC pic32cm5164jh01100-soc: cortex-m0 standing in for the M0+ (CPUID
  overridden to 0x410CC601), 32 IRQs, OR gates for shared vectors, NVM
  rows ROM, IOBUS aliases. Board pic32cm-jh01-cpro.
- qtest pic32cm-jh-test (12 cases) and board documentation.

Known gap: MPU_TYPE reads 0 because QEMU only creates pmsav7-dregion for
Armv7 cores; a cortex-m0plus CPU type is needed for the M0+ MPU.

Peripheral Pretender downstream patch; not for upstream submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
